// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_lnx_cap_setgid.yml
// ID Sigma: 3a716279-c18c-4488-83be-f9ececbfb9fc
// Título: Linux Setgid Capability Set on a Binary via Setcap Utility
// Descripción: Detects the use of the 'setcap' utility to set the 'setgid' capability (cap_setgid) on a binary file.
This capability allows a non privileged process to make arbitrary manipulations of group IDs (GIDs), including setting its current GID to a value that would otherwise be restricted (i.e. GID 0, the root group).
This behavior can be used by adversaries to backdoor a binary in order to escalate privileges again in the future if needed.

// Fecha de creación: 2026-01-24
// Fecha de modificación: 
// Aplica a: Producto: linux | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: linux
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: low
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\linux\process_creation\proc_creation_lnx_cap_setgid.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/setcap" and ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_setgid"
